1
00:00:00,967 --> 00:00:01,900
<i>I didn't notice anyone
chasing me,</i>

2
00:00:02,033 --> 00:00:03,200
<i> so I think I'm safe.</i>

3
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:04,833
<i>This is me, Joey. This is Peter.</i>

4
00:00:04,967 --> 00:00:06,400
<i> Where did you get this video?</i>

5
00:00:06,533 --> 00:00:08,133
<i> In the alley in Purok Uno.</i>

6
00:00:08,267 --> 00:00:11,367
<i>My uncle and I installed
the CCTV on the main street.</i>

7
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,733
<i> If you're hiding something,</i>

8
00:00:12,867 --> 00:00:15,000
<i>now is the right time
to tell us.</i>

9
00:00:15,133 --> 00:00:18,000
<i> Did you tip Major Delgado?</i>

10
00:00:18,133 --> 00:00:19,367
<i> Golda?</i>

11
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,367
<i>I didn't even get a thank-you
gift for the tip I gave you?</i>

12
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:23,800
<i> Whose drugs did we intercept?</i>

13
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:25,833
<i>A name popped up in my contacts.</i>

14
00:00:25,967 --> 00:00:26,800
<i> Executioner.</i>

15
00:00:26,933 --> 00:00:28,067
<i>What are you working on
right now?</i>

16
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,733
<i>I'm planning to investigate
the drug transport</i>

17
00:00:30,867 --> 00:00:32,733
<i>that was intercepted in Bolagos.</i>

18
00:00:32,867 --> 00:00:33,867
<i> Miguel is a problem.</i>

19
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,167
<i> He's a block in our system.</i>

20
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:36,533
<i> In a chess game,</i>

21
00:00:36,667 --> 00:00:38,600
<i>what do you do with a piece
that is an obstacle to the plan?</i>

22
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:39,533
<i> Knocked down.</i>

23
00:00:39,667 --> 00:00:41,167
<i> Doesn't she look familiar?</i>

24
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:42,533
<i> I think I've seen her before.</i>

25
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:43,267
<i> Bingo!</i>

26
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:44,700
<i> We have another problem.</i>

27
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:45,833
<i> This.</i>

28
00:00:45,967 --> 00:00:47,000
<i>What are you planning
to do with the video?</i>

29
00:00:47,133 --> 00:00:48,200
<i> Don't tell me you'll post it.</i>

30
00:00:48,333 --> 00:00:49,800
<i> We'll get there, but not now.</i>

31
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:51,733
<i> Do you need treatment?</i>

32
00:00:51,867 --> 00:00:53,100
<i>I'm just here
to ask you something.</i>

33
00:00:53,233 --> 00:00:56,667
<i>What is your relationship
with Major Miguel Delgado?</i>

34
00:01:42,667 --> 00:01:46,967
<i>Found a body or a missing
person?</i>

35
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:49,833
<i> So far, there's none, Joey.</i>

36
00:01:49,967 --> 00:01:53,100
<i>Usually, it's just kids
and seniors.</i>

37
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:54,833
<i> Why? What's the problem?</i>

38
00:02:00,733 --> 00:02:02,667
Who are you really, Mister?

39
00:02:04,733 --> 00:02:07,500
And you too, Miss,
who are you really?

40
00:02:16,067 --> 00:02:17,167
Okay, fine.

41
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,200
Okay?

42
00:02:20,333 --> 00:02:21,733
Okay, Madam.

43
00:02:21,867 --> 00:02:23,133
Madam...

44
00:02:23,267 --> 00:02:24,467
Matias...

45
00:02:26,333 --> 00:02:27,833
I'm begging you.

46
00:02:30,933 --> 00:02:33,600
What do you need from me?

47
00:02:35,167 --> 00:02:37,300
Didn't you say you couldn't
betray us?

48
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:39,367
Okay.

49
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,233
Let's prove your loyalty.

50
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:44,700
Where's his cell phone?

51
00:03:00,667 --> 00:03:01,933
Hello, Ramon?

52
00:03:02,067 --> 00:03:04,100
<i> Major, we need to meet.</i>

53
00:03:05,167 --> 00:03:06,233
Where are you?

54
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:09,767
Here in...

55
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:11,600
Ramon!

56
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:12,600
Ramon!

57
00:03:20,967 --> 00:03:21,767
Madam...

58
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:26,233
Have mercy, Madam.

59
00:03:27,467 --> 00:03:29,267
Have mercy on my family, Madam.

60
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:31,000
Matias,

61
00:03:31,133 --> 00:03:32,067
help me.

62
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:35,000
Madam, have mercy on me, Madam?

63
00:03:35,133 --> 00:03:36,467
Madam!

64
00:05:05,733 --> 00:05:07,233
He said he wanted to talk
to me,

65
00:05:07,367 --> 00:05:08,800
but right now,
I can't contact him.

66
00:05:09,933 --> 00:05:12,000
Something bad might happened
to him.

67
00:05:16,467 --> 00:05:19,800
<i>Your number cannot be completed
as dialed. Please...</i>

68
00:05:21,333 --> 00:05:25,533
Golda, this is Ramon,
Staff Sergeant Ramon Orbos...

69
00:05:25,667 --> 00:05:28,000
Did your contacts mention
something?

70
00:05:29,767 --> 00:05:33,800
Miguel, I told you everything
that I know!

71
00:05:33,933 --> 00:05:35,900
I don't want to get involved
anymore.

72
00:05:36,067 --> 00:05:39,433
Don't you want to get involved
because you're hiding something?

73
00:06:09,367 --> 00:06:11,033
<i> Why do you seem nervous?</i>

74
00:06:11,167 --> 00:06:14,900
<i>There's another name mentioned
by my contacts,</i>

75
00:06:16,067 --> 00:06:18,567
<i> and it's not Ramon Orbos.</i>

76
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:19,933
<i> So who is it?</i>

77
00:06:20,967 --> 00:06:22,300
<i> You, Miguel.</i>

78
00:06:23,567 --> 00:06:26,033
<i>You're on the syndicate's radar.</i>

79
00:06:28,033 --> 00:06:30,733
<i> So be careful.</i>

80
00:06:30,867 --> 00:06:32,833
<i> They will come after you.</i>

81
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,533
It's dawn already.

82
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:47,533
- Where did you come from?
- Love.

83
00:06:50,467 --> 00:06:52,667
I just followed up on a case.

84
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:58,167
Go get some rest.

85
00:07:04,067 --> 00:07:05,000
How about you?

86
00:07:07,467 --> 00:07:09,533
I'm not sleepy anymore.

87
00:07:09,667 --> 00:07:11,200
I'll just follow.

88
00:07:46,233 --> 00:07:53,633
Who is that?

89
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:54,967
What happen?

90
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:10,933
<i> Joey...</i>

91
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:12,833
Joey...

92
00:08:14,433 --> 00:08:16,600
Joey, the door, open that door,
Joey.

93
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:21,933
<i> Joey...</i>

94
00:08:25,933 --> 00:08:26,967
<i> Joey!</i>

95
00:08:29,267 --> 00:08:30,533
Peter?

96
00:08:30,667 --> 00:08:32,367
- Joey, I'm outside.
- Why?

97
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:34,033
Open that door, open it.

98
00:08:35,167 --> 00:08:35,867
Joey...

99
00:08:39,267 --> 00:08:40,233
Joey...

100
00:08:43,167 --> 00:08:44,400
What is it?

101
00:08:46,167 --> 00:08:46,900
Joey...

102
00:08:49,933 --> 00:08:50,767
Check this out.

103
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,300
Remember that guy you filmed in
the alley?

104
00:09:09,267 --> 00:09:11,400
Make sure not to contaminate
the crime scene.

105
00:09:11,533 --> 00:09:12,700
Okay, Sir.

106
00:09:24,633 --> 00:09:27,033
Major, is the victim
a policeman?

107
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:30,200
That's Ramon Orbos, right?

108
00:09:30,333 --> 00:09:32,067
One of the checkpoint
police officers

109
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:36,033
who inspected the drug-laden
truck that you intercepted.

110
00:09:37,633 --> 00:09:40,733
He had injuries on his body,

111
00:09:40,867 --> 00:09:42,833
so it looks like he was tortured

112
00:09:42,967 --> 00:09:44,600
before he was completely
silenced.

113
00:09:44,733 --> 00:09:48,133
Major, do you have any idea,
Major, who did this?

114
00:09:49,933 --> 00:09:51,267
Major...

115
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:52,033
Major...

116
00:09:52,167 --> 00:09:54,067
Do you know Golda Briones?

117
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:05,400
<i>Here in the grassy part of
the Bypass Road,</i>

118
00:10:05,533 --> 00:10:07,633
<i>boundary of Bolagos and Amaroso,</i>

119
00:10:07,767 --> 00:10:09,933
<i>the body of a person identified</i>

120
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:12,700
<i>as Police Staff Sergeant
Ramon Orbos was found.</i>

121
00:10:12,833 --> 00:10:15,833
<i>It will be remembered that Orbos
was one of the station police</i>

122
00:10:15,967 --> 00:10:17,200
<i>who inspected the truck
that was seized</i>

123
00:10:17,333 --> 00:10:21,400
<i>by the Bolagos Police containing
illegal drugs.</i>

124
00:10:21,533 --> 00:10:24,067
He was involved in Father's
drug bust case.

125
00:10:25,467 --> 00:10:28,133
Isn't there a big syndicate
behind that?

126
00:10:28,267 --> 00:10:30,733
Couldn't his death have
something to do with it?

127
00:10:32,567 --> 00:10:33,500
It's possible.

128
00:10:45,533 --> 00:10:46,200
Why?

129
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:51,800
I posted the video on FlipTok.

130
00:10:51,933 --> 00:10:55,300
Oh my, Joey, are you serious?

131
00:10:55,433 --> 00:10:57,933
Joey, it's dangerous,
especially since this happened!

132
00:10:58,067 --> 00:10:59,600
What are you doing?

133
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:06,367
Major, do you know
Golda Briones?

134
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,767
I don't know her.

135
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:13,333
Weird, Major,

136
00:11:14,533 --> 00:11:17,200
because what she told me
is so different.

137
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:20,100
What do you know about Golda?

138
00:11:21,933 --> 00:11:24,533
She told me everything, Major.

139
00:11:26,533 --> 00:11:28,000
Stay away from her.

140
00:11:28,133 --> 00:11:30,800
Stop your investigation.

141
00:11:30,933 --> 00:11:34,400
Major, I'm a reporter.

142
00:11:34,533 --> 00:11:38,000
My job is to find out
and expose the truth.

143
00:11:38,133 --> 00:11:39,200
Truth?

144
00:11:39,333 --> 00:11:41,133
Is that really your goal?

145
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:42,767
Or is it just so you can say
something?

146
00:11:44,133 --> 00:11:45,367
Stop bothering me!

147
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:57,767
Joey, what you did was so wrong.

148
00:11:57,900 --> 00:11:59,667
What if that syndicate
tracked you down?

149
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:00,433
What if?

150
00:12:00,567 --> 00:12:02,233
That's why I'm deleting it now!

151
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:06,233
Of course, I didn't use my real
account, right?

152
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:15,967
There, it's okay.

153
00:12:16,133 --> 00:12:18,467
Even the account? Is it deleted?
Are you sure?

154
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:20,300
Yes, everything, deleted.
I also double-checked.

155
00:12:23,900 --> 00:12:26,033
It's a good thing there
are almost no viewers.

156
00:12:27,367 --> 00:12:30,500
You know, Joey, I told you
from the start

157
00:12:30,633 --> 00:12:32,800
that you should have told
your father this.

158
00:12:42,033 --> 00:12:46,200
Blunt force trauma to his wrist
and jawline.

159
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:49,267
Multiple contusions
and lacerations:

160
00:12:49,433 --> 00:12:51,933
classic signs of torture.

161
00:12:52,067 --> 00:12:54,133
But his cause of death,

162
00:12:54,267 --> 00:12:55,833
single gunshot wound.

163
00:12:58,133 --> 00:13:01,067
Contact range, here in his right
temporal lobe.

164
00:13:02,533 --> 00:13:04,067
Approximate time of death?

165
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:08,867
Judging from rigor and lividity,
between 1 and 2 AM.

166
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
But, Sir,

167
00:13:10,133 --> 00:13:12,500
there were no defensive wounds.

168
00:13:12,633 --> 00:13:15,167
He was probably restrained
the whole time.

169
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:18,633
It seems Personal,
not just salvaged.

170
00:13:18,767 --> 00:13:19,900
Agree, Sir.

171
00:13:20,033 --> 00:13:22,000
Where are his personal effects?

172
00:13:22,167 --> 00:13:24,233
- Here, Sir. Just a moment.
- Good.

173
00:13:27,867 --> 00:13:28,700
Here it is.

174
00:13:48,967 --> 00:13:50,933
Mother, I've been calling Father
for a while

175
00:13:51,067 --> 00:13:52,900
but he's not answering.

176
00:13:53,033 --> 00:13:55,167
<i>You're not used to your Father.</i>

177
00:13:55,333 --> 00:13:57,967
<i>You know you can't bother him
at work.</i>

178
00:13:58,100 --> 00:14:00,400
Just call him later.

179
00:14:00,533 --> 00:14:02,800
<i> What time is your class?</i>

180
00:14:02,933 --> 00:14:04,300
I don't have class today.

181
00:14:04,433 --> 00:14:06,567
I'm going home.
I need to talk to Father.

182
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:08,833
Why, Joey? Did something happen?

183
00:14:08,967 --> 00:14:11,867
I'll tell you later, Mother,
when I get there.

184
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,233
I'll update you
when I'm on the bus, Mother.

185
00:14:15,267 --> 00:14:18,933
Okay. Be careful, my child,
okay? Love you.

186
00:14:19,067 --> 00:14:20,500
I love you.

187
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:29,400
Come in.

188
00:15:32,967 --> 00:15:34,433
Sir.

189
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,567
Sit down.

190
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:39,300
Sir, you called for me.

191
00:15:39,433 --> 00:15:41,833
I also wanted to report
something to you.

192
00:15:41,967 --> 00:15:45,133
Sergeant Orbos' preliminary
autopsy is out.

193
00:15:45,267 --> 00:15:47,667
He had multiple blunt traumas.

194
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:50,167
He also had a gunshot wound
to the head,

195
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:51,733
at close range.

196
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:53,300
Execution style.

197
00:15:53,433 --> 00:15:55,500
This is not the work
of amateurs.

198
00:15:55,633 --> 00:15:58,733
Someone used enhanced
interrogation tactics

199
00:15:58,867 --> 00:16:01,367
before he was completely
silenced.

200
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:04,000
His personal belongings were
also recovered

201
00:16:04,133 --> 00:16:06,133
including his cell phone.

202
00:16:08,567 --> 00:16:09,733
<i> Hello, Ramon?</i>

203
00:16:09,867 --> 00:16:13,067
<i> Major, we need to meet.</i>

204
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:14,933
<i> Where are you?</i>

205
00:16:15,067 --> 00:16:19,433
Where were you between 1 to 2 AM
last night, Major Delgado?

206
00:16:32,333 --> 00:16:33,567
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

207
00:16:33,700 --> 00:16:36,700
I'm near the bus station,
Mother.

208
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:00,200
Good morning, Ma'am.

209
00:17:00,333 --> 00:17:03,600
Has anyone updated your CCTV
system?

210
00:17:03,733 --> 00:17:05,267
System update?

211
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:07,933
That's not from the village.
That's personal use.

212
00:17:08,067 --> 00:17:10,500
We installed that for
our bakery.

213
00:17:19,933 --> 00:17:20,900
Andrew.

214
00:17:22,133 --> 00:17:23,167
Final cue.

215
00:17:24,533 --> 00:17:26,567
Are we dropping the expose
today?

216
00:17:29,933 --> 00:17:30,800
Let's burn it.

217
00:17:32,367 --> 00:17:33,467
Copy.

218
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:34,800
Kyle, standby.

219
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:38,867
And...

220
00:17:40,467 --> 00:17:47,300
we are live in five, four,
three. Music up. Two...

221
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:57,500
Fellow Tirada, let's not play
around the bush anymore.

222
00:17:57,633 --> 00:17:59,667
Let's get straight
to the agenda.

223
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:04,767
You all remember the Bolagos
drug bust operation, right?

224
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:09,467
P800 million pesos worth
of illegal narcotics

225
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:10,633
were intercepted.

226
00:18:10,767 --> 00:18:13,000
Heroic work, some people say.

227
00:18:13,133 --> 00:18:17,233
But now that Staff Sergeant
Ramon Orbos is dead,

228
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:27,367
tortured and executed,
the smell is even more pungent.

229
00:18:30,733 --> 00:18:32,300
Here's a kicker.

230
00:18:32,433 --> 00:18:35,300
We may have another cop
on the take,

231
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,633
a high-ranking one.

232
00:18:39,767 --> 00:18:44,467
Major Miguel Delgado.

233
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:49,600
Is he really a hero or just
greedy for money?

234
00:18:52,233 --> 00:18:53,700
Father?

235
00:18:53,833 --> 00:18:55,133
- Father?
- Joey.

236
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:56,967
Mother...

237
00:18:57,100 --> 00:18:59,100
Your father is still not home.

238
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:04,433
He still doesn't answer
my calls.

239
00:19:04,567 --> 00:19:09,833
Maybe he's just busy
at the station or somewhere.

240
00:19:10,967 --> 00:19:12,367
Wait a minute,
have you eaten yet?

241
00:19:13,533 --> 00:19:16,500
I'll just prepare food for you.
Wait a minute, okay?

242
00:19:16,633 --> 00:19:18,233
Just sit there.

243
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:24,200
Peter?

244
00:19:24,333 --> 00:19:26,133
<i>Hello? Joey, are you home
already?</i>

245
00:19:26,267 --> 00:19:27,600
Yes, I just got home. Why?

246
00:19:27,733 --> 00:19:30,867
I've been reading about
drug bust cases in Bolagos.

247
00:19:31,033 --> 00:19:34,433
<i>I've heard reports and read
about your father, Joey.</i>

248
00:19:34,567 --> 00:19:36,667
You need to see this.
I'll send you the link.

249
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:37,600
Okay.

250
00:19:48,167 --> 00:19:50,833
Major Miguel Delgado.

251
00:19:50,967 --> 00:19:53,600
Yes, he was the one who ended

252
00:19:53,733 --> 00:19:56,967
the controversial drug bust
operation in Bolagos.

253
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:58,467
Great, right?

254
00:19:58,600 --> 00:20:01,400
But is he really a hero?

255
00:20:02,467 --> 00:20:05,600
Is he the clean cop he claims
to be?

256
00:20:05,733 --> 00:20:08,100
Or is he also a member
of the syndicate

257
00:20:08,233 --> 00:20:10,733
and just pretending to be
a Saint?

258
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:24,467
These are not fake, Fellow
Tiradas.

259
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:27,067
These are not AI-generated.

260
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,933
Do you see this girl right here?

261
00:20:29,067 --> 00:20:32,500
Her name is Golda Briones.

262
00:20:32,633 --> 00:20:36,500
She herself confirmed to me
about her secret affair

263
00:20:36,667 --> 00:20:38,067
with Major Delgado.

264
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:41,767
Why does Major Delgado know the
details of the drug shipments?

265
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:43,867
Because he is the protector
of the syndicate.

266
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,100
And once he gets that
protection money,

267
00:20:46,233 --> 00:20:48,133
he will double-cross them.

268
00:20:49,633 --> 00:20:53,133
That's the kind of cop
Major Delgado is.

269
00:20:53,267 --> 00:20:56,700
A traitor, a crook,
and an immoral person.

270
00:21:01,867 --> 00:21:04,100
Mother, let's not watch this
anymore.

271
00:21:04,233 --> 00:21:06,300
There's no truth to what he's
saying.

272
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:10,633
And how can you believe it?

273
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:11,667
If that's true,

274
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:13,833
we should have been rich
for a long time now.

275
00:21:15,533 --> 00:21:19,233
And this Andrew Dizon,
he's just mad at the police.

276
00:21:19,367 --> 00:21:22,433
Did you know? At school,
he insulted Father.

277
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:26,533
Mother, maybe we should
just wait for Father

278
00:21:26,667 --> 00:21:30,567
because I'm sure he has an
explanation for what's going on.

279
00:21:31,900 --> 00:21:35,667
There's nothing clearer
than the photos I saw, Joey.

280
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:43,200
Your Father is fooling us.

281
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:12,400
Hey, hey!

282
00:22:12,533 --> 00:22:14,367
Are you really not going
to stop lying?

283
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:15,333
This is for you.

284
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:17,600
You are placed under preventive
suspension

285
00:22:17,733 --> 00:22:19,200
pending full investigation.

286
00:22:19,333 --> 00:22:21,267
Have you shown your Father
the video

287
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:22,633
of the police officer
who was killed?

288
00:22:22,767 --> 00:22:25,800
You know, I'm sure your Father
will find a way

289
00:22:25,933 --> 00:22:27,833
so you'll be complete again.
I'm sure.

290
00:22:27,967 --> 00:22:28,933
Good morning.

291
00:22:29,067 --> 00:22:32,233
We need to recover a recorded
video.

292
00:22:32,367 --> 00:22:35,200
Peter, who updated the systems
in Purok Uno?

293
00:22:35,333 --> 00:22:36,733
It looks like the clean-up
was selective.

294
00:22:36,867 --> 00:22:39,167
Something is being hidden,
and something is being erased.
